      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_0db53f222c12c97403b59c568d62f189e49f008671964115c50f176309219eb0",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The zero-divisor structure has two opposed roles: its complementary idempotents make bicomplex arithmetic and holomorphic reconstruction componentwise, but loss of invertibility when either component vanishes enlarges the scalar pole at 1 to the translated noninvertible locus and forces infinite-product convergence to require an invertible limiting product.",
